## Forbidden

White screen is **forbidden**. Also forbidden: empty · black · null · broken · crash · undefined · infinite loading · empty component.

## Pre-render (all must PASS)

DATA · COMPONENT · UI · PAGE · ROUTES · IMPORTS · AUTH · API · PREVIEW · VIEW  

All PASS → render real page.  
Any FAIL → **do not** render white screen.

## Allowed only

1. Real page  
2. Skeleton page  
3. Error component (`FailClosedPanel`)  
4. Temporary message  
5. Self-recovery page  

## Self recovery

Fail → skeleton/placeholder → retry → recover → load real UI.  
Never crash. Never blank.

Examples: Inbox / Pay Now / Image (`SafeImage` placeholder) / Messages.

## Owner sees white screen → automatic

CERTIFICATION FAIL · SPRINT FAIL · COMMIT BLOCKED · PUSH BLOCKED · FREEZE BLOCKED · OWNER APPROVAL BLOCKED

## Absolute law

White screen must never reach Owner · Buyer · Seller · Admin · Super Admin · Preview · Production.  
If white screen exists → **the product does not exist.**

Final law: No white / empty / null screen. Only real page · skeleton · self recovery · error component.

Child law: Priority 0 Absolute Law (`lib/priority-0-v1.ts`) — nothing comes before white screen + preview + Conversation Hub.

## Cursor must never

- Ship blank/crash routes  
- Skip skeleton / fail-closed / `SafeImage` fallbacks  
- Treat missing data as empty DOM with no recovery UI  
- Claim PASS when Owner can see a white screen on preview
